    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0404" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 P.W./1–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-22T13:00:00-05:00">January 22, 1946—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>678. For Hodgson. Urtels 177, Jan 7, and 303, Jan 10. Australian Legation note
                    received Jan 21 forwards “First List of Major Japanese War Criminals”<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d304-f1"/> and “proposes that question of final determination
                    of list of accused for trial be handled by Far Eastern Commission”.</p>
                <p>Australian Govt, has nominated Chief Justice Sir William Webb as Judge and Mr.
                    Justice Mansfield as Associate Prosecutor for International Military Tribunal in
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Dept. does not consider War Crimes Commission should proceed at this time with
                    listing or charging with crimes against the peace or humanity as proposed in
                    Australian list in view of Australian proposal this matter be dealt with in Far
                    Eastern Commission. Moreover, it is understood Prosecution Agency established at
                    MacArthur’s headquarters, to which all nine signatories of the surrender
                    instrument and Philippines and India are nominating Associate Prosecutors, has
                    been given responsibility of determining list of major war criminals charged
                    with crimes against the peace. This list of defendants will be first group
                    brought before International Military Tribunal shortly to be established in
                    Tokyo. Copy of Charter of this tribunal which <pb facs="0405" n="393"
                        xml:id="pg393"/> has been issued in Tokyo<anchor n="6" xml:id="d304-f2"/>
                    will be forwarded as soon as received in Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d304-f1" n="5" xml:id="d304-f1-content">
